            <div xml:id="d671">

                <pb facs="0771" n="673" xml:id="pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3143: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-16T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 16,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 18—10:30
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>442. My 388, November 18th, 5 p.m. Ministry of Finance expresses gratitude for
                    action of bank, states that rise in value of gold has so diminished customs
                    surplus that latter insufficient repay amount due but repayment will be effected
                    in first few days January from salt surplus.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
